WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.288
Today, the Chinese-speaking world spans many places.

00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:07.757
Taiwan, mainland China, Hong Kong and Macau each have their own character.

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:10.647
Airplanes connect Chinese communities far away.

00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:13.719
Singapore also has many people who use Chinese.

00:00:13.953 --> 00:00:17.167
Overseas Chinese communities are spread all over the world.

00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:20.877
In hawker centers, familiar aromas drift through the air.

00:00:21.158 --> 00:00:24.482
Some places use traditional characters, others use simplified characters.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.590
The same word is said a bit differently in different places.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.613
Many children learn Chinese at school.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.790
They connect with friends far away through the internet.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.970
One storybook can be read in different accents.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.776
At festivals, Chinese people everywhere celebrate together.

00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:46.044
Food and customs show a rich diversity.

00:00:46.044 --> 00:00:49.587
Red lanterns hang all over the lively streets.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:53.853
Different histories have created a diverse Chinese-speaking world.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:57.760
Learning Chinese is also learning these stories.
